    "q-133765": {
      "dom_id": "step-q133765",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224903/assets/99cd0af2bcfd5148a49179203b6fff4831133d875fda9fa474d928eab5eb8f1c.png)\n\nWhat is the slope of the trend line shown above.",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(4,1)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(8,9).$\n\nTherefore, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-1}{8-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
