    "q-134012": {
      "dom_id": "step-q134012",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224903/assets/60b546c0e2d37362fefde1023ed093d2f544b187742bb690d5fe60bc417b48d4.png)\n\nWhat is the slope of the trend line shown above?",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(1,2)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(3,5).$\n\nTherefore, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5-2}{3-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-134012-a",
              "type": "math",
