    "q-134011": {
      "dom_id": "step-q134011",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224903/assets/c55d326b26a8bb6831f38456b7b47878ef66a185090c7327cbb151c4e951be33.png)\n\nWhat is the slope of the trend line shown above?",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(3,2)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(5,1).$\n\nTherefore, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-2}{5-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
