      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224903/assets/2ddf870155c876bac41bd437229afb971bcb6eb6cdd67351c27a0132f7d05325.png)\n\nEstimate the slope of the trend line for the scatter plot above. Round your answer to the nearest $0.5.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's draw an approximate trend line for our scatter plot:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14224903/assets/b79dacf04634d91eae5ee8dd82a6603ed93357d6300a95e6343a683429caf506.png)\n\nIt seems that the trend line passes through $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})≈(4,6)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})≈(8,4).$\n\nTherefore, we estimate the slope $m$ of the line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ≈\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-6}{8-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{4} \\\\  & =-0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
